course: dictionary
lesson: 3922
title: Frostbite: an injury from the cold
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Frostbite is a noun, the name of an injury. The clues are in the words around it: «Wet clothes lose heat fast, so fingers and toes can get frostbite.» Cold, wet clothes and fingers and toes all point to freezing cold harming the body.
explain: The sentence «Frostbite makes skin white or greyish and numb» tells you what it looks like. Numb means you cannot feel anything there. Frostbite is damage to skin and the body under it, caused by very cold weather.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into a sentence: «Frostbite can damage fingers, toes, ears and noses in the cold.» Frostbite can damage fingers and toes in the cold makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: Frostbite is an injury to the skin and the body under it, caused by very cold weather.
fact: It usually happens on fingers, toes, nose and ears.
fact: First the skin may go red and tingly, then it can turn white or grey and numb.
fact: Wet clothes make frostbite happen faster, so keep dry and wear warm layers.
fact: If you think someone has frostbite, get an adult, warm the area gently and do not rub it.
exercise: «Wet clothes lose heat fast, so fingers and toes can get frostbite.» What is frostbite? | A cold wind that blows over mountains | A warm hat that keeps you dry | A bite from an animal in the snow | *An injury to skin caused by very cold weather
exercise: Which parts of the body does frostbite usually affect? | Back and shoulders | Hair and eyebrows | *Fingers, toes, nose and ears | Knees and elbows
exercise: «Frostbite makes skin white or greyish and numb.» What does numb mean? | Covered in thick fur | Loud and noisy | *Unable to feel anything | Hot and sweaty
test: How can you help prevent frostbite in cold weather? | Rub your fingers with snow | Stay out in wet clothes all day | *Wear hats, gloves, scarves and warm socks | Eat ice cream outside
test: If someone has frostbite, what should you use to warm the skin gently? | *Warm, not hot, water | Snow | A campfire held right against the skin | Hot water from the kettle
exam: Golden snub-nosed monkeys live in snowy mountain forests in China. What may help prevent frostbite on their noses? | Living near the sea | Eating only hot food | *Their tiny upturned noses | Having no fur at all
